From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Michals <tcmichals@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: sunxi: sun55i-pck600: fix backpointer, detect initial state, and power on USB2

The sunxi PCK-600 driver has two critical bugs preventing power domains
from functioning correctly:

1. pd->pck = pck was never assigned in sunxi_pck600_probe(), causing
   a NULL-pointer dereference if sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power() fails
   and logs via pck->dev.
2. pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, false) unconditionally hardcoded
   is_off = false. This informed the Linux PM domain core that all
   domains were already active at boot. In hardware silicon, domains like
   domain 8 (USB2 at 0x07068000) are in state 0x0 (PPU_POWER_MODE_OFF).
   Consequently, when consumer devices such as dwc3 probe and attach,
   genpd skips calling power_on(). The DWC3 core MMIO registers remain
   unpowered, returning 0x00000000 (GSNPSID), which aborts probe with:
   "dwc3 6a00000.usb: this is not a DesignWare USB3 DRD Core".

Fix both issues by:
- Storing pd->pck = pck.
- Reading actual hardware state from PPU_PWSR to initialize is_off.
- Explicitly powering on PD_USB2 and marking it GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON
  so the DWC3 controller, USB 2.0 PHY, onboard FE1.1S hub, and AIC8800
  Wi-Fi are active and stay powered across runtime PM transitions.
- Adding diagnostic dev_info prints for each power domain during probe.

Signed-off-by: Tim Michals <tcmichals@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
@@ -164,14 +164,34 @@
 
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_domains; i++) {
 		struct sunxi_pck600_pd *pd = &pck->pds[i];
+		u32 pstate;
+		bool is_off;
 
+		pd->pck = pck;
 		pd->genpd.name = desc->pd_names[i];
 		pd->genpd.power_off = sunxi_pck600_power_off;
 		pd->genpd.power_on = sunxi_pck600_power_on;
 		pd->base = base + PPU_REG_SIZE * i;
 
 		sunxi_pck600_pd_setup(pd, desc);
-		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, false);
+
+		pstate = readl(pd->base + PPU_PWSR);
+		is_off = (FIELD_GET(PPU_PWR_STATUS, pstate) != PPU_POWER_MODE_ON);
+
+		if (!strcmp(desc->pd_names[i], "USB2")) {
+			ret = sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power(pd, true);
+			if (ret)
+				dev_err(dev, "failed to power on USB2 domain: %d\n", ret);
+			pd->genpd.flags |= GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON;
+			is_off = false;
+		}
+
+		dev_info(dev, "domain \"%s\" (id %d) pstate=0x%x, %s%s\n",
+			 pd->genpd.name, i, readl(pd->base + PPU_PWSR),
+			 is_off ? "off" : "on",
+			 (pd->genpd.flags & GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON) ? " [always-on]" : "");
+
+		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, is_off);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to initialize power domain\n");
 			goto err_remove_pds;
-- 
